WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.940
More Stability for Your Kicks

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.940
Take a holiday!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.030
<i>The train is approaching the platform.</i>

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.920
<i>Please stand behind the yellow line.</i>

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.610
<i>Hiyoshi. This station is Hiyoshi.</i>

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.940
We've got a game!

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.550
Settle down.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.140
I'm so excited... sir.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.330
Yeah, yeah. It's very exciting.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.950
Why do you look so glum, Tree Trunk?

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.180
N-No reason.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:49.020
<b>Keijo High School</b>

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.020
So this is Keijo, huh?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.020
Wow!

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:54.840
<b>Episode 3
What's Most Important</b>

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.070
Shut up.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.020
We already told you that you're not 
getting a run out, short stuff.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.360
What did you call me?!

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.360
Now, now. Don't fight.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.020
Here. You can have this.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.000
You just want me to carry your stuff.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.060
It's all good, man.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.830
I guess we got here a little too early.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.590
Sekizan!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.650
Huh?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.010
You're not him.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.870
Huh? What?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.090
How annoying...

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.750
Taira, can we get changed 
in our usual place?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.430
You're already thinking
about the game, Sekizan?

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.840
Aren't you going to say 
"long time, no see" to me?

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:33.560
No.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.340
Sekizan!

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.440
I'll show you the way!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.110
Not necessary.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.240
Who the heck was that?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.570
Keijo's vice-captain.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.710
Come to the south field when you're changed.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.580
Hurry, hurry. As quick as you can, please!

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.630
He hasn't changed, has he?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.920
The third-years are already used to him.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.430
Attention...

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.890
I'll now announce our starting lineup.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.900
They're here.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.930
Hisakawa, thanks for having us today.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.890
No, thank you.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.130
For two whole years...

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:42.300
I've been waiting for this.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:50.700
Our time has finally come, Sekizan.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.100
Enough talk!

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.390
Let's do this.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.810
Are you starting?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.260
Yeah...

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.760
I-Is your shoulder—

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.100
As you can see, it's fine.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.230
Why don't I get to play?!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.610
That tree trunk is playing!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.820
Put me in!

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.570
Hey, you...

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.590
M-Miyuki-kun...

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.250
Who are you calling a tree trunk?

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.920
What?

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:02.420
Are you making fun of Sumiaki?

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.850
Miyuki-kun...

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.710
You may not know this yet, 
but this guy's amazing.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.090
It's not like that...

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.240
You'll understand once you see him play.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:25.320
(Prop)
<b>1 Otsuka Taku</b>

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.320
Vice-captain (Hooker) 
<b>2 Taira Tadakazu</b>

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.320
<b>Keijo</b>

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.320
Captain (Prop)
<b>3 Hisakawa Kumio</b>

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:25.320
(Lock)
<b>4 Ochiai Keita</b>

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.320
(Lock)
<b>5 Tanashi Yugo</b>

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:25.320
(Flanker)
<b>6 Arai Sukeyuki</b>

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.320
(Flanker)
<b>7 Masa Ikue</b>

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:29.320
(Number Eight)
<b>8 Honkawa Tatsuaki</b>

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:29.320
(Scrum-half)
<b>9 Miya Tokumitsu</b>

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.320
(Fly-half)
<b>10 Miyuki Atsushi</b>

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:29.320
(Wing)
<b>11 Ogi Yoichi</b>

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.320
(Center)
<b>12 Shimoi Tokio</b>

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:29.320
(Center)
<b>13 Kanai Shunya</b>

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.320
(Wing)
<b>14 Musashi Yukichi</b>

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.320
(Fullback)
<b>15 Fushimi Yuzuharu</b>

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:33.330
(Prop)
<b>1 Shinshi Yutaka</b>

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.330
Vice-captain (Hooker)
<b>2 Hachioji Mutsumi</b>

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:33.330
(Prop)
<b>3 Hirota Eiichi</b>

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.330
(Lock)
<b>4 Kashima Koichiro</b>

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:33.330
(Lock) 
<b>5 Iwashimizu Sumiaki</b>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:33.330
<b>Jinko</b>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:33.330
Captain (Number Eight)
<b>8 Sekizan Takuya</b>

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:37.330
(Flanker) 
<b>6 Hyosu Shinnosuke</b>

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.330
(Flanker)
<b>7 Kasuga Hirokuni</b>

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.330
(Scrum-half)
<b>9 Kamo Raita</b>

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.330
(Fly-half) 
<b>10 Oharano Etsugo</b>

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:37.330
(Wing) 
<b>11 Maroudo Kosuke</b>

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:37.330
(Center) 
<b>12 Takebe Tomomichi</b>

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.330
(Center) 
<b>13 Ise Natsuki</b>

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.330
(Wing) 
<b>14 Suwa Yusaku</b>

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.330
(Fullback)
<b>15 Kibi Shota</b>

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.420
I'll kill him.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.700
After how much you squabbled 
over one spot, this is pitiful.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.340
By the way, Gion, have you studied the rules?

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.860
Yeah, I have.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.990
You can't throw the ball forward,
and you can't drop it.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.970
If that's all you learned, I'll hit you.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.940
Keijo to kickoff.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.760
Knock-on by Jinko.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.830
That's when they drop the ball forward.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.330
Yeah. Now, they have a scrum.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:28.080
I am the world's greatest!

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.630
The one and only,
the famous hooker: Taira Tadakazu.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.970
You won't beat me, Hachi.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.890
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.390
Saying that always pumps me up.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:44.010
Iwashimizu, push as hard as you can.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:44.900
Okay.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.400
Crouch.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:48.990
Bind.

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:51.150
Set.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.760
<i>The eight of them together 
are as strong as a boulder.</i>

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.290
The ball's out!

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:06.210
I don't enjoy being outdone 
by another first-year.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.410
<i>Which side will he try to pass me on?</i>

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.390
<i>What? Straight through me?</i>

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.730
Forwards, get back!

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.270
Kibi, nice tackle!

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.860
That was close.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.090
Hey, is Keijo's team strong?

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:39.000
What?!

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.870
Well, I guess you wouldn't know any better.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:49.360
Keijo's been a regular Kanagawa Prefecture
 semifinalist for the past few years.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.970
Last year, they even gave the champions
a run for their money.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.760
All of their players have played rugby before.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.100
Iwashi!

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.420
<i>P-Pass...</i>

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.570
Knock-on by Jinko.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.200
Your decision-making's 
too slow, Iwashimizu.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.530
S-Sorry...

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.290
Set!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.380
Iwashimizu, push harder next time!

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.680
O-Okay...

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.400
Jinko's #5 sucks!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.180
Target him!

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.460
Hey, you dumb midget.
What's wrong with the giant?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.650
"Dumb midget"?

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.770
He's useless.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.460
Are you making fun of Sumiaki?

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:12.410
They've been pressuring us 
for close to ten minutes.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.740
We need to reverse the flow of the game.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.050
Their #10 in particular 
is causing us problems.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.930
Oh, no! He got through.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:26.600
Stop him, Iwashimizu!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.470
Give me everything you've got, Sumiaki.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:16.980
Try!

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:27.400
Sumiaki...

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.890
Are you making fun of me?!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:47.680
You don't deserve to be on the field 
if you can't even attempt a tackle on me.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.600
You're just a giant eyesore.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:55.820
Get off the field.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:04.700
Keijo

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.610
What the heck is he doing out there?!

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.200
I'll take his place!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.960
You idiot! You can't play lock.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.520
Then, I'll play in place of 
Hachi-senpai instead—

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:14.960
Ow...

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:16.800
Are you stupid?

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.460
Stop throwing a tantrum!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.220
I want to play.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:34.230
For now, just do whatever you can from here.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.310
<i>I can't play even though I want to.</i>

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:43.980
<i>So why's he doing nothing
when he gets the chance to play?</i>

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:48.120
Hey, Tree Trunk!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.370
Why are you just standing there?!

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.620
That's our ball he's got!

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.670
<i>This is our ball!</i>

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:53.930
It's ours.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.280
Knock-on by Keijo.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:05.790
So you've finally woken up, 
have you, Iwashimizu?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.510
Yes, sir.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.000
<b>Are you making fun of Sumiaki?!</b>

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.000
<b>Are you making fun of me?!</b>

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.380
The ball's ours! Attack!

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.180
Iwashi, come short!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:44.060
Great! It's that idiot again!

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.530
I'll knock him fl—

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:51.950
He's so strong.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.410
Penalty to Keijo.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.500
"Over the top."

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.590
You're not allowed to prevent 
the ball from being played.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.050
Gion, the ball's been kicked out.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:19.540
What happens now?

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:25.620
Uh, the big guys jump 
and try to win the ball?

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.740
That's right. A line-out.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.690
Good job.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.830
Yeah!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.910
You throw the ball in between two lines—
your team's and your opponent's, right?

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:43.880
Why can't you just throw it to
 a teammate? They fouled us.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.430
Because rugby is a gentleman's sport.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.390
Even after a foul,

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:51.880
both teams are given
the opportunity to regain possession.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.730
<i>#5 will definitely jump for the ball.</i>

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.860
It's too high!

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:09.110
I know what you're planning!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.540
<i>H-He caught it one-handed?</i>

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.790
His size sure makes him dependable.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.010
Matsu-san.

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:39.250
After all, rugby is a physical sport.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.020
Hisakawa's coming!

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.520
All right!

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:49.520
They turned the ball over!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:58.870
You punk!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.620
Nice, Hirota!

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:11.710
Nice pass!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.290
It's not fair.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.850
Keijo's a private school powerhouse.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.740
Well-built athletes, assembled through
middle school recommendations,

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.200
get to train in an ideal environment.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:32.110
We can't beat Keijo for physicality.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.310
But...

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:41.250
physical ability isn't the most 
important quality in rugby.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:58.950
What's most important is the 
ability to overcome your fear...

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:04.650
and charge full force into 
opponents bigger than yourself.

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.540
Those eyes...

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.090
They haven't changed since two years ago.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.780
I fell in love with those eyes.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:39.300
I'm so excited for my 
first game with Keijo!

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:43.730
Captain, is the Jinko team 
we're playing today strong?

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:46.660
They're weaklings.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:51.690
We wanted to play another team, 
but our schedules didn't line up.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.820
Hello.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.060
Hey!

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:58.320
Let's have a good game today.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.530
We have first-year novices with us, too.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.610
So go easy on us, guys.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:24.220
Keijo

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.220
Private schools are so strong!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:33.480
If it hadn't been raining,
we could've kept them under 100 points.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.400
They even have showers here.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.730
What? Wow.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.990
What's wrong with that pack of losers?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.290
Now, now, Taira-kun...

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.310
Their losing ways will rub off on us!

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.250
I refuse to play against them ever again!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.490
I didn't think they'd be that bad.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.570
The game ended more than an hour ago.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.860
What's your name?

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.300
Sekizan Takuya.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:21:02.070
<i>No matter how badly your team lost,
 it never dampened your spirits.</i>

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:11.490
When you look at me like that, 
I just have to crush you!

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:20.070
I started playing rugby in high school, too.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:26.030
I thought I was training as hard as Taku,
but I was fooling myself.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:36.820
He was the only one who could even come 
close to competing with the other schools.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:43.730
But you can't do it alone.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:54.330
Unless all 15 guys on the field want 
to win, you're not playing rugby.

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:02.340
I want to win with Taku.

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:12.490
We need to start by changing 
the flow of the game.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "What Should I Do?"</b>

00:23:45.780 --> 00:23:48.790
Next time: "What Should I Do?"
